{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nReplaying a candidate change tells you *what would change*, not whether it is *better*. The store already carries outcome signals needing no LLM/human labeling: revise→re-review pairs, verdict flips on byte-identical material (the reviewer-noise floor), bug closes with `close_class=plan_defect`, `caused_by` links, PASS-then-completion-FAIL tickets, reopens.\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py` (celestine-treasonous-ewe, closed): `build_corpus(store_roots, *, cache_dir) -> manifest` recovers `plan_review_result_v1/v2` sidecars, verifies material, writes `cache_dir / f\"{manifest['content_hash']}.jsonl\"` — one JSON line per VERIFIED row ONLY, fields `store, ticket_id, review_event_ts, review_event_uuid, schema, verdict, ticket_type, description, file_impact, file_impact_scope, no_file_impact_reason, children, material_fingerprint, verified, generation, reconstructed, ran_model`. No per-ticket rows in the manifest itself.\n\n`corpus._enumerate_event_blobs` applies NO content-type filter — it returns EVERY event blob, deduped by `(ticket_id, uuid)`. `_CONTENT_TYPES` filtering happens one layer up, in `corpus._load_ticket_events`. A caller wanting other kinds (STATUS/COMMENT/COMPLETION_VERDICT) filters `_enumerate_event_blobs`'s own output by `kind`.\n\nEvery event `ts` is a `time.time_ns()` NANOSECOND epoch value; convert with `datetime.fromtimestamp(ts / 1e9, tz=timezone.utc)`, matching `rebar_reconciler/conflict_bug_filing.py:119`.\n\nSTATUS events carry `data = {status, current_status, ...}`. `clean_close`'s timestamp is the `ts` of the MOST RECENT STATUS event with `data[\"status\"] == \"closed\"`. A `COMPLETION_VERDICT` event's TYPE covers BOTH outcomes — `data.schema == \"completion_verifier_fail_v1\"` marks FAIL, `\"completion_verifier_pass_v1\"` marks PASS — filter on `data.schema`, not the event kind.\n\nEach surfaced finding carries `criteria: list[str]` (may name >1 criterion, e.g. `[\"E2\",\"T8\"]`).\n\n`config.tracker_dir_override()` reads `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`, winning verbatim over any config. `caused_by` is an OUTBOUND edge on the SOURCE (bug) pointing at TARGET (culprit); inbound only on the culprit (`include_inbound=True`).\n\n`mine_outcome_corpus.py` (docs-tree, not importable from `src/`) defines `reopen_count`/`force_close`/`completion_verifier_fail_count` as pure functions over a per-ticket event dict.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py`:\n\n- **Corpus identity + ticket population**: `corpus.build_corpus(store_roots, cache_dir=...)`; `manifest[\"content_hash\"]` is the hash labels key to. Read `cache_dir / f\"{content_hash}.jsonl\"` for `(store, ticket_id)` pairs, `review_event_ts`/`review_event_uuid`/`verdict`/`material_fingerprint` — the single driver for every label; unverified rows never enter labels. Refuses (raises, naming both hashes) on a hash mismatch against a supplied `labels-<hash>.jsonl`.\n- **Finding-level source (verified-only)**: per cache row's `review_event_uuid`, re-read that SAME `REVIEW_RESULT` blob's `data` via `corpus._enumerate_event_blobs` + `_batch_cat` (matched by uuid). Filter `findings` to `sidecar.surfaced_findings(data)` before any `norm_id` join.\n- **Ticket-level event source (multi-store, env override)**: per `store_name, tracker_git_root` in `store_roots`, temporarily set `os.environ[\"REBAR_TRACKER_DIR\"] = tracker_git_root` (restored `finally`) around `show_ticket(ticket_id, include_inbound=True)`. `reopen_count`/`force_close`/`completion_verifier_fail_count` REIMPLEMENTED in `labels.py` (mirroring the miner), fed by `corpus._enumerate_event_blobs` filtered to `kind in {STATUS, COMMENT, COMPLETION_VERDICT}` then `_batch_cat`; `completion_verifier_fail_count` further filters to `data.schema == \"completion_verifier_fail_v1\"`. Same STATUS events supply `clean_close`'s timestamp.\n- **Ticket-level labels**: `escaped_defect(X)` = (a) `X.close_class == \"plan_defect\"` OR (b) `X.inbound_deps` has `relation == \"caused_by\"`. `completion_failed_after_pass(X)`: a PASS cache row at ns-ts T AND a `completion_verifier_fail_v1` event with `ts > T`. `reopened` (`reopen_count > 0`); `escape_signals(X) = escaped_defect OR completion_failed_after_pass OR reopened OR force_close`; `clean_close` = closed AND NOT escape_signals AND `(now - datetime.fromtimestamp(latest_close_ts / 1e9, tz=timezone.utc)).days >= CLEAN_CLOSE_MIN_DAYS` (constant, default 7). Each label carries source event id(s).\n- **Finding-level labels**: per ticket's cache rows ordered by ts, each CONSECUTIVE pair (k, k+1) with differing `material_fingerprint`. Finding `f` in k: `f.norm_id` also in k+1 → `persisted`; absent from k+1 → `resolved_by_author`. New in k+1 → neither. `noise_flip` only over IDENTICAL-material pairs, comparing `verdict`.\n- **Noise floor**: (a) verdict flip rate; (b) per-criterion churn — a finding's `norm_id` is a member of EVERY criterion in its `criteria` list; `churn(c) = 1 - jaccard(S_k(c), S_{k+1}(c))`; published figure = mean over every criterion observed, plus per-criterion breakdown. (c) per-question Pass-2 agreement — `verification = {\"binary\": {...}, \"severity_attributes\": {...}}`; flatten as `\"binary.<key>\"`/`\"severity_attributes.<key>\"`; compare keys present in both findings; agreement = matches/total, pooled, with comparison count.\n- Output `labels-<content_hash>.jsonl` + Markdown report, joined to `content_hash`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/labels-report-<date>.md` (new)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_labels.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: five-ticket synthetic corpus exercising each label — a bug via `close_class`, a separate origin via `inbound_deps`; `completion_failed_after_pass` true only for a `completion_verifier_fail_v1` event after a PASS (not for `pass_v1`); `clean_close` false when any escape signal fires, using the LATEST close STATUS ts converted from ns; finding present-then-absent → `resolved_by_author`; present-in-both → `persisted`; new → neither; a two-criteria finding contributes to both churn sets; identical-material flip via `noise_flip` only; a permanently-dropped finding excluded from the join; per-question agreement over nested `verification` (one match, one mismatch → 0.5); an UNVERIFIED row never reaches a label. Empty corpus → empty report. Stale-hash file refused.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every review/finding in the verified corpus carries the labels above, with source event ids. Evidence: `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_labels.py` (75/75, mutation-verified) proves every label-derivation rule; `build_labels` was additionally run end-to-end against a real 40-ticket subset of the \"rebar\" tracker (11 verified rows / 9 tickets), producing a committed `labels-b3784f0609e3d7f7dcd5a20f2d83081bc37c31dfddd62e2bf8f0baeb3eed8ad6.jsonl` + report -- this caught a real production-data bug (explicit-null `verification`, fixed with a regression test). A full-corpus (~6400-ticket) run is DEFERRED follow-up: each ticket needs its own `show_ticket` call, too slow at that scale under the store's current activity (confirmed per-call cost, not lock contention, since an isolated local clone made no difference).\n- [x] The noise floor is published with the identical-material pair count. Evidence: unit tests for each metric, plus the committed subset report's pair-label section (2 differing-material pairs in the 40-ticket subset; `noise_flip` itself is unit-tested directly since the subset had no identical-material pair).\n- [x] Labels are keyed to `corpus.build_corpus(...)[\"content_hash\"]`; the loader raises on a stale hash. Evidence: `test_load_labels_refuses_a_stale_hash`; the committed report's filename embeds its content hash.\n- [x] No LLM calls. Evidence: all tests and the real subset run used zero provider credentials; the module makes no LLM/network calls anywhere."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788081505382160132,"uuid":"494648df-a224-4201-8a5c-85c51984074f"}